    "result_text": "There is one test class and it passes, with the full build green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`, replacing the three separate telephone / email / household checks with one whole-key comparison that rejects with 409 only on an exact full-key match.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `identityKey` string field to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and it's returned on create and read).\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n  - `addOwner` now builds the owner, assigns `householdId` (when `sharesHousehold`), then runs a single `rejectDuplicateIdentity(owner)` check \u2014 removing the old separate telephone/email/household rejections and the `!sharesHousehold` gate.\n  - Added `identityKey(Owner)` (canonical telephone + normalized email-or-empty + householdId-or-empty) and `rejectDuplicateIdentity(Owner)` (compares the whole key against every existing owner).\n  - `toOwnerDtoWithDerivedFields` now populates `identityKey`.\n  - Removed the now-dead `rejectDuplicateTelephone`, `rejectDuplicateEmail`, `rejectDuplicateHousehold`, and `householdKey` methods (kept `canonicalizeHousehold`/`householdId`, still used to derive the shared household id).\n\n- **`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException.java`** \u2014 New exception carrying the colliding key; deleted the three old `DuplicateOwner{Telephone,Email,Household}Exception` classes.\n\n- **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 Replaced the three old 409 handlers/constants with a single `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 409 handler (`errors: [\"identityKey\"]`).\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Ignored `identityKey` in `toOwnerDto` (it's set by the controller, like `bulkSignupWarning`).\n\n**Behaviour:** Because telephone is part of the key, two household members (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different identity keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The new acceptance test (`coreRejectsIdentityCollision`) and the full build pass.",
